    "updated_at": "2015-10-16T12:09:05Z",
    "body": "Probably not completely a duplicate? If we do\n\n> It, ~~and its ::backdrop pseudo-element,~~ are not rendered if its inclusive ancestor has the display property set to none.\n\nThen it is not clear whether the pseudo-element should be rendered if the top layer element has `display: none`, because `::backdrop` doesn't seem to be a descendant of the element, does it?\n",
